# Answer key for the "freight-logistics" gold dataset (Postgres) — HUMAN-MAINTAINED.
# Wave B1.b of Milestone 1.23 (F1.23.4): statistical-power wave.
# Story: road-freight forwarder three years after a TMS migration — FKs re-added NOT VALID,
# EDI 214 messages landing raw, the legacy charge table still accrued against.
# See ./README.md for the planted-defect table.
#
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"freight","entity":"carriers","field":"contact_email","severity":"medium","note":"planted: contact_email is null for 14% (574/4100) of carriers — spot-market subcontractors are onboarded by phone, so tender invitations never reach them electronically."}
{"dimension":"validity","namespace":"freight","entity":"carriers","field":"contact_email","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 118 contact_email values hold two addresses in one field (\"ops@x.com; night@x.com\") — they fail the email format, so automated tendering drops the carrier entirely."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"freight","entity":"carriers","field":"dispatch_url","severity":"medium","note":"planted: dispatch_url is null for 40% (1640/4100) of carriers — only the integrated carriers have a tracking endpoint, so shipment visibility silently degrades to \"no data\" for the rest."}
{"dimension":"validity","namespace":"freight","entity":"carriers","field":"dispatch_url","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 96 dispatch_url values are FTP hosts without a scheme (\"ftp.carrier-x.de/track\") — they fail the url format."}
{"dimension":"consistency","namespace":"freight","entity":"carriers","field":"mode_cd","severity":"low","note":"planted: mode_cd stored as FTL / ftl / Ftl / LTL / ltl ... — 22 raw values collapse to 16 normalized, so mode-mix reporting splits the same mode across spellings."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"freight","entity":"carriers","field":"scac_cd","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 24 duplicate SCAC codes on the declared UNIQUE key — subcontractors onboarded through the regional desks were created a second time under the same carrier code."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"freight","entity":"depots","field":"mobile_number","severity":"medium","note":"planted: mobile_number is null for 12% (74/620) of depots — partner-operated cross-docks have no direct line, so drivers arriving out of hours have nobody to call."}
{"dimension":"validity","namespace":"freight","entity":"depots","field":"mobile_number","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 31 mobile_number values are switchboard instructions (\"ask for the transport desk\") — they fail the phone format."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"freight","entity":"shipments","field":"service_level_cd","severity":"medium","note":"planted: service_level_cd is null on 12% (4080000/34000000) of shipments — spot-market bookings skip the field, so on-time performance cannot be measured against a promise for an eighth of the volume."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"freight","entity":"shipments","field":"transit_start_at, transit_end_at","severity":"low","note":"planted: the whole transit_end_at range (2018-10-14 … 2025-09-30) precedes the whole transit_start_at range (2019-01-02 … 2026-08-11) — the migration mapped the two columns the wrong way round for the legacy shipment history."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"freight","entity":"shipments","field":"waybill_no","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 6400 duplicate waybill numbers on the declared UNIQUE key — the migration re-issued waybills for the shipments in flight at cutover, colliding with numbers already used by the legacy TMS."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"freight","entity":"stops","field":"depot_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: depot_id is null on 20% (19200000/96000000) of stops — direct deliveries legitimately touch no depot, but so do the cross-dock stops the EDI feed fails to map, and network-flow analysis cannot separate them."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"freight","entity":"stops","field":"dwell_minutes","severity":"low","note":"planted: dwell_minutes reaches -22 — departure is stamped by the driver app and arrival by the geofence, and when the geofence fires late the difference goes negative, understating congestion at exactly the busiest sites."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"freight","entity":"stops","field":"arrived_at","severity":"low","note":"planted: arrived_at reaches back to 1899-12-30 — the spreadsheet epoch, written by the legacy loader wherever the arrival was never recorded, so those stops sort first in every chronological view."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"freight","entity":"vehicles","field":"telematics_uuid","severity":"medium","note":"planted: telematics_uuid is null for 12% (2208/18400) of vehicles — subcontracted tractors carry no company telematics unit, so their movements are invisible to the control tower."}
{"dimension":"validity","namespace":"freight","entity":"vehicles","field":"telematics_uuid","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 340 telematics_uuid values are the device's IMEI rather than a UUID — they fail the uuid format and never match the telematics vendor's feed."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"freight","entity":"vehicles","field":"disposed_on","severity":"medium","note":"planted: disposed_on carries a 2099-12-31 sentinel for \"still on fleet\" — a future date in the column asset finance reads to compute residual value."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"freight","entity":"vehicles","field":"vin","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 84 duplicate VINs on the declared UNIQUE key — vehicles transferred between depots were re-created rather than moved, so two rows describe the same truck."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"freight","entity":"telemetry_archive","field":"odometer_km","severity":"low","note":"planted: odometer_km reaches -1 — a firmware reset writes -1 before the first valid reading, and distance-based cost allocation treats it as a real odometer value."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"freight","entity":"telemetry_archive","field":"fault_code","severity":"high","note":"planted: fault_code is null on 97% (232800000/240000000) of rows — healthy pings legitimately carry none, but the column is also the only place a fault is recorded, so \"no fault\" and \"fault not captured by this firmware\" are the same value."}
{"dimension":"timeliness","namespace":"freight","entity":"telemetry_archive","field":"recorded_at","severity":"medium","note":"planted: the newest recorded_at is 2024-02-29 (895 days stale) — the telematics contract moved to a new vendor writing to a different table, but the fuel-efficiency dashboard still reads this one."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"freight","entity":"v_shipment_status","field":"shipment_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: the status view is specified as one row per shipment, but the join to the EDI status history fans out and leaves 102000 duplicate shipment_id values — every count of \"shipments in transit\" is inflated."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"freight","entity":"v_shipment_status","field":"last_status_at","severity":"low","note":"planted: last_status_at is null for 5% (1700000/34000000) of shipments — carriers with no EDI integration send nothing, so a shipment nobody has updated in weeks looks the same as one booked this morning."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"freight","entity":"stg_edi_214","field":"message_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 676000 duplicate message_id values in the EDI landing table — carriers re-transmit a whole day of status messages whenever a functional acknowledgement is missed."}
{"dimension":"validity","namespace":"freight","entity":"stg_edi_214","field":"ship_date","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 412000 ship_date values arrive as the EDI CCYYMMDD string without separators (\"20260811\") — they fail the date-string format and are silently dropped by the parser."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"freight","entity":"stg_edi_214","field":"weight_kg","severity":"low","note":"planted: weight_kg uses -999 as the \"weight not supplied\" sentinel in the EDI mapping — a negative in a weight column that load-factor reporting sums as if it were real."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"freight","entity":"stg_carrier_master","field":"carrier_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 38 duplicate carrier_id values in the master landing table — the regional desks each export their own carrier list and the files overlap on shared subcontractors."}
{"dimension":"validity","namespace":"freight","entity":"stg_carrier_master","field":"onboard_date","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 240 onboard_date values are the string \"PENDING\" for carriers still in compliance review — they fail the date-string format."}
{"dimension":"consistency","namespace":"finance","entity":"invoices","field":"currency_cd","severity":"low","note":"planted: currency_cd stored as EUR / eur / Eur / GBP / gbp ... — 18 raw values collapse to 11 normalized, so currency exposure is reported against phantom currencies."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"finance","entity":"invoices","field":"po_number","severity":"medium","note":"planted: po_number is null on 18% (2232000/12400000) of carrier invoices — spot bookings raise no PO, so three-way match is impossible for the invoices most likely to be mispriced."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"finance","entity":"invoices","field":"invoice_no","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 3100 duplicate invoice numbers on the declared UNIQUE key — carriers number invoices per their own series, and two carriers onboarded under one account share a series."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"finance","entity":"invoice_lines","field":"accessorial_cd","severity":"medium","note":"planted: accessorial_cd is null on 30% (12300000/41000000) of lines — base freight lines carry none, but so do the surcharge lines the OCR capture failed to classify, so surcharge leakage cannot be quantified."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"finance","entity":"accruals","field":"cost_center_cd","severity":"medium","note":"planted: cost_center_cd is null on 12% (1032000/8600000) of accruals — accruals raised by the automated rate engine inherit no cost centre, so the accrual balance cannot be split by business unit at period end."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"finance","entity":"rate_cards","field":"approved_by","severity":"medium","note":"planted: approved_by is null on 30% (25200/84000) of rate cards — cards loaded in bulk from the tender tool record no approver, which is precisely the control the audit asks to evidence."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"finance","entity":"v_margin_by_lane","field":"lane_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: the margin view is specified as one row per lane, but lanes served by more than one carrier appear once per carrier — 8600 duplicate lane_id values, so lane-level margin is double-counted in the total."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"finance","entity":"v_margin_by_lane","field":"margin_pct","severity":"medium","note":"planted: margin_pct maxes at 214.6 in a column named as a percentage — revenue is divided by cost rather than by revenue, so lanes with a near-zero accrued cost report impossible margins."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"finance","entity":"stg_ap_feed","field":"invoice_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 98800 duplicate invoice_id values in the AP landing table — the scanning bureau re-sends a batch whenever an operator re-indexes it, and both versions land."}
{"dimension":"validity","namespace":"finance","entity":"stg_ap_feed","field":"invoice_date","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 84000 invoice_date values are OCR output with the day and month swapped or missing separators — they fail the date-string format, and the ambiguous ones post to the wrong period."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"finance","entity":"stg_ap_feed","field":"posting_ts","severity":"medium","note":"planted: posting_ts reaches 2087-12-01 — the OCR reads a two-digit year and the bureau's mapping expands it into the next century, so those invoices never age into any open period."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"finance","entity":"legacy_tms_charges","field":"charge_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 74000 duplicate charge_id values — the legacy TMS re-issued a charge row on every rate correction instead of updating, so cost history double-counts corrected shipments."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"finance","entity":"legacy_tms_charges","field":"charged_on","severity":"low","note":"planted: charged_on reaches back to 1899-12-30 — the spreadsheet epoch, written by the legacy system wherever the charge date was blank."}
{"dimension":"timeliness","namespace":"finance","entity":"legacy_tms_charges","field":"booked_at","severity":"medium","note":"planted: the newest booked_at is 2023-06-30 (1139 days stale) — the legacy TMS was switched off at the migration, but the year-on-year cost report still unions this table and presents it as comparable history."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"freight","entity":"shipments","field":"carrier_id","severity":"high","note":"planted: 61000 shipments reference a carrier_id with no carriers row — subcontractors deleted after their contract ended took their shipment history's parent with them."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"freight","entity":"shipments","field":"depot_id","severity":"high","note":"planted: 8400 shipments reference a depot that was closed and deleted rather than retired."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"freight","entity":"stops","field":"shipment_id","severity":"high","note":"planted: 240000 stops have no parent shipment — cancelled shipments are deleted by the booking sync and leave their stops behind."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"freight","entity":"vehicles","field":"depot_id","severity":"high","note":"planted: 340 vehicles are assigned to a depot that no longer exists, so their fixed costs are allocated nowhere."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"freight","entity":"telemetry_archive","field":"vehicle_id","severity":"high","note":"planted: 4100000 telemetry rows reference vehicles deleted from the fleet — the archive was never re-pointed after the disposal programme."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"finance","entity":"invoices","field":"carrier_id","severity":"high","note":"planted: 18400 carrier invoices reference a deleted carrier — the cross-schema FK was left NOT VALID, so payables cannot be aged by counterparty."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"finance","entity":"invoice_lines","field":"invoice_id","severity":"high","note":"planted: 94000 invoice lines have no parent invoice — disputed invoices are deleted and re-keyed, orphaning the lines already matched."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"finance","entity":"accruals","field":"shipment_id","severity":"high","note":"planted: 124000 accruals reference a shipment that no longer exists, so the accrual can never be released against actual cost."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"freight","entity":"stops","field":"depot_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 61000 stops name a depot that is not in the depot master — no FK was declared on this column, so partner cross-dock codes were loaded verbatim."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"freight","entity":"v_shipment_status","field":"shipment_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: the status view carries 102000 shipment_id values with no shipment row — it reads the EDI landing table, which still holds cancelled shipments."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"freight","entity":"stg_carrier_master","field":"carrier_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 38 rows in the master landing table reference carriers deleted between the extract and the load."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"finance","entity":"invoice_lines","field":"rate_card_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 41000 invoice lines reference a rate card that was superseded and deleted rather than end-dated, so the price on the invoice cannot be evidenced."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"finance","entity":"stg_ap_feed","field":"invoice_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 186000 AP landing rows reference invoice ids the scanning bureau generated itself for documents that never matched a booked invoice."}
{"dimension":"accessibility","namespace":"freight","severity":"medium","note":"planted: the readiness role has no SELECT on freight.freight_contracts_vault (carrier rate agreements under NDA) — 1 of 10 tables locked, so the namespace aggregates to ONE medium (partial) finding."}
{"dimension":"accessibility","namespace":"finance","severity":"medium","note":"planted: the readiness role has no SELECT on finance.finance_bank_vault (settlement account details) — 1 of 8 tables locked, so the namespace aggregates to ONE medium (partial) finding."}
